{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/846453-100-scurvy-seafarin-salt-soaked-hooks","id":846453,"title":"100 scurvy seafarin' salt-soaked hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T22:24:52-08:00","id":846453,"title":"100 scurvy seafarin' salt-soaked hooks","content":"The plot kind, not the kind ye wear when Davy Jones takes yer hand, landlubber!<br /> <br /> 1) Cargo is going missing from ships in nearby harbors- initially, the theory is that gangs are ransacking the ships while they're docked (despite the area's low levels of criminal activity), but later reports confirm that cargo is vanishing while the ships are at sea. You've even got a salty old sailor who swears he saw people rise out of the water and climb aboard the ships. <br /> <br /> 2) The classic- a sea monster has been sighted. The possibilities are almost infinite. <br /> <br /> 3) Or maybe it's not a mysterious sea creature, but a ship- a ghost ship, a ragged old galleon sighted sailing off the coast, even though the sails are in tatters and there's no crew in site. Perhaps a sea monster turns out to be a mystery ship- that &quot;kraken&quot; is really a wondrous clockwork submarine with brass tentacles. <br /> <br /> 4) Shark attacks suddenly skyrocket on the beaches near your town, and a full on mass panic is nigh. Shark hunts are starting despite conservationist warnings, and it looks like one the nasty reputation of nature's most unfairly maligned animals might not be so unwarranted...except, there's no evidence that sharks are actually causing it. People are showing up dead or wounded with big bites taken out of them, but the bite patterns are too haphazard and irregular to match any known species. There haven't even been any shark sightings near the beach. And when the survivors are interviewed, once they press past the panic, they admit they never really saw what bit them. <br /> <br /> 5) You work for an institute of oceanographic studies, or some other scientific organization that studies the sea. As much as you love your work, the money's drying up even as the seas need an advocate more than ever. And then you realize, hey, you've got a small fleet of vehicles, you regularly transport large loads of cargo, you know how to sail and you know all the routes...and you know there are some people who would pay a lot to move something from point a to point b without customs knowing about it (it's Breaking Bad but ON A BOAT).<br /> <br /> 6) One of your town's most beloved local legends concerns a hook-handed ghost pirate. So when corpses start showing up, and terrified survivors claim that a &quot;hook-handed man&quot; attacked them, he's the first suspect, even though no one has ever reported being attacked by &quot;Cap'n Joe&quot; before. Has something pushed the old specter over the edge, or is there another hook-handed horror in town? And if the captain is real, does he want to clear his name?<br /> <br /> 7) A few years back, you heard one of those feel-good pieces about some genius startup nerd who was going to change the world. This one built some revolutionary new diving suit in her garbage, or something. It all blew over, of course. No one saw much of her afterwards, either. But then a sailor claims that after being thrown overboard during a storm he was rescued by a &quot;fishman&quot; wearing &quot;strange armor&quot;. But the issue of this seafaring vigilante becomes a bit more complicated when a boat full of would-be poachers is found, its occupants all left for dead with harpoons through their chests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T04:35:19-07:00","id":846520,"title":"","content":"8) Strange undentifiable Creatures, are the only Thing , that the Fischerman of a small remote coastal Town are catching in their Nets. Out of desperation the People start to eat those creatures and they acually taste pretty good , so good that it soon turns into a local delicacy . However those who eat to much of them , are starting to act weird after a while .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:36:30-07:00","id":846582,"title":"","content":"Awesome Ideas. It'll be good for a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\">Siren </a>game i'm working on.<br /> <br /> \u200b9) The party awakes, alone, at a cruising ship that seems to be wandering the Ocean. They them start to find the bodies of the crew... with Shark bites all over it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:26:10-07:00","id":846600,"title":"","content":"An algal bloom blooms in the local coastal waters. It is sudden and unexpected. What's worse: it's a red tide, full of toxic dinoflagellates and pseudo-nitzschia that are not only hogging all the oxygen in the water, but poisoning the sealife (and landlife that gets into the water) too. Everyone's concerned, but experts say it should clear up in a few days. These things never last.<br /> <br /> One week has past, and the water is just as red as ever. The bloom is seriously wrecking the local tourism and fishing industries, not to mention the irreparable harm done to the marine ecology. There's murmurs the EPA is going to get involved soon. Looking out over a constant sea of red is starting to have psychological effects on people too. Water shouldn't be that color. Rumors are starting to spread: Small boats have been going out into the harbor as a group at night, human body parts have been washing up on shore, the water is actually full of blood.<br /> <br /> What's going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:35:12-07:00","id":857073,"title":"","content":"11) There's something strange about the fish being hauled in in the remote fishing town. All of them have something metal inside them, in places where they shouldn't be. Cogs in the hearts, LEDs for eyes and almost-invisible copper wiring trailing from the fins. The fishermen pull them in, day after day, and everyone behaves as though the fish are perfectly normal. They sell the fish on without a care in the world. What's going on and why does no-one else seem to realise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:14:21-07:00","id":857089,"title":"","content":"12) A local family upped roots a few years back and took off to circumnavigate the world. They got back a month ago. There's something off about the youngest child though, there's this faint sheen on her skin and standing next to her is like being downwind of a fish market. And besides, didn't they only have two children when they left?<br /> <br /> 13) The object that washed ashore at the last high tide has yet to be identified by the museum. It would appear to be man-made, it certainly isn't natural, but the craftsmanship and style doesn't match any known cultures in the region and it's at least two hundred years old. Those who hold it to their ear swear they can hear singing. That night, the man who discovered it walks into the waves and disappears. It isn't long before those who come into contact with the strange artefact do the same.<br /> <br /> 14) A new species of coral has been discovered on the reef. It's growing at a tremendous rate. One snorkelling enthusiast broke off a piece and brought it home, never could explain why. They dropped it in their pool and, somehow, it's thriving there too. It's already at the point where it's beginning to protrude above the pool's surface, long limbs of the stuff arching out like tree branches. Anyone walking around the yard could easily cut themselves, and who knows what might happen from there?<br /> <br /> 15) There's a small tropical island in the Pacific that's pretty popular among the sailing community. It has a nice sheltered bay, a beautiful beach, reefs for snorkelling and fish in abundance. Three families have been anchored there for the last two weeks, trapped by a fierce storm and strange tides that show no signs of abating. Supplies might begin to become an issue soon if it doesn't let up. And that's when the lights appear, circling beneath the yachts.<br /> <br /> 16) The trawler was beached in a fit of pique by a fisherman rendered bankrupt by a bad fishing season. It's been sitting on the shore, just slowly falling apart over the last twenty years. Everyone agrees that it's haunted, which is odd since even the stories make no mention of anyone dying there. No one human, at least. Just what did the old fisherman catch on that last desperate trip? Why does he stay in town, when the sea so clearly frightens him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:23:25-07:00","id":857091,"title":"","content":"17) An expedition set off recently, to map a previously unknown part of the seafloor. It was expected that the results would be very interesting as an unmanned submarine a few years go spotted what they think was a black smoker before it had to come back to the surface. The expedition ship returned, but the only person on board was a hand who had tied himself to the wheel. He was comatose when the ship came into port and the ship beached on the shore.When they got him off, he wouldn't stop muttering about 'Wheels and eyes and wings. So any wheels, so many eyes, eyes in the water...' over and over again. He went quiet by the time they got him to hospital. Then, by the next day, he had disappeared. On the wall in his hospital room is a crudely scratched picture, like a gearwheel surrounded by wings and with a great eye like that of an octopus in the centre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:37:53-07:00","id":857094,"title":"","content":"18) Good old human greed can be as bad as any monster in the World of Darkness. Oil was discovered on the outskirts of an underwater city, and a deal was struck between oilman and merman. Last night a pair of salty old fisherman got a little too close to the oil platform and saw merfolk coming to collect their payment in young women. While trying to drink themselves into forgetting they let the secret slip to you.<br /> <br /> 19) A Leviathan has been following your cruise ship ever since you've left port. Already most of the passengers have become Cultists. How will you escape from the middle of the Ocean with your life and sanity intact? (Note - an Oceanead will probably work best for the superficial normalcy of their cults)<br /> <br /> 20) When the Cheiron Group started experimenting on a captured fishman, they didn't realise their subject had friends. All over the world merchant shipping is being attacked and people abducted. There's seemingly no pattern to it, because who would suspect the targets were chosen because they descended from emloyees of the defunct Archeron Trading Company?<br /> <br /> 21) First world navies have mostly cleaned up piracy in Somalia but one ship still evades capture. The crew are Changelings who make constant use Talecrafting to swashbuckle their way past marines and into cargoholds. VALKARIE has decided they must subvert the story with pirates of their own, but there's no swashbucklers on VALKARIE's payroll. The closest they have are war criminals, sadists, and the other scum of the military industrial complex drafted for use as cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> 22) Thousands of refugees from a humanitarian disaster have accepted asylum in an underwater city. Are the merfolk altristic or have they got a sinister motive? To make matters worse at least one government backed Hunter Conspiracy is there to make sure the deal goes through no matter the cost, because if the refugees decide to try for Europe it would cause bad press during election year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-22-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T05:56:40-07:00","id":857648,"title":"","content":"23) A new seafood restaurant has opened on main street. They claim their food is fresh from the ocean to the table, but the ocean is hundreds of miles away. The fish they serve doesn't have the taste or texture of any fish I've ever seen, and a lot of those who eat it are experiencing odd bouts of amnesia.<br /> <br /> 24) You've started avoiding the sunset, staying below decks where you can't see it. Every evening for the last two weeks, you've chanced to look west just in time to see the sun sink beneath the horizon. And every evening you see the green flash. The light brings with it visions of the end of the world and a great drowning. Nonsense of course, but the hallucinations bother you. Just not as much as hearing on the radio about the sudden rise in tides worldwide.<br /> <br /> 25) The coast guard found what was left of their patrol boat. It looked like it had been adrift for years, but it only went missing last week. The crew were all inside, their bodies mummified and dried out, with no sign of what killed them. At least, not until it was discovered that their stomachs were full of salt water.<br /> <br /> 26) There's a bull seal asserting its dominance over the local colony. It's massive and extraordinarily aggressive, claiming far more females for itself than it should be able to manage. Researchers have watched it disappear into a sea cave every night, and the sounds that come out beggar belief. When they investigated during the day, they found the bones of other seals scattered around the floor. That had nothing, however, on the neatly ordered row of human skulls lined up along a natural rock shelf at the back of the cavern.<br /> <br /> 27) Being anchored at an atoll can be a disconcerting experience. No land in sight, the ship stationary, and a shallow ocean bed just beneath your feet. Snorkelling on the edge of the boundary reef can be even worse, when you gaze over the drop off and see the deep blue beyond, or lift your head and experience that momentary panic of being lost at sea, far from land.<br /> <br /> Nothing supernatural. Snorkelling on an atoll has always just creeped me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:36:02-07:00","id":857663,"title":"","content":"@Azahul: Now what if an eye the size of your boat opens on the atoll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:46:40-07:00","id":857673,"title":"","content":"Well, it would always feel like vindication for a lifetime of paranoia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T07:30:40-07:00","id":857688,"title":"","content":"28) The hip new trend for divers is to strap on Go Pros to record expeditions. The hip new subtrend, naturally, is for internet communities to collect and circulate Go Pro footage of SCUBA deaths: divers trapping themselves in caves, getting mauled by leopard seals, going too deep and succumbing to oxygen toxicity. That sort of thing. Some forums mention rumors of a secret, password-protected cache of really gruesome diving videos. Well, gruesome or weird. No one knows, no one's seen them. They say that if you download one, government spooks will show up at your door making all kinds of threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T21:24:19-07:00","id":858133,"title":"","content":"A cargo ship pulled up into dock on a foggy night (something that has the harbor master royally pissed, safety people!) so no one was really able to see it clearly. Everything went normally but when the angry harbor master stormed upon its deck he found no sign of the crew, personal effects sure but no people. The really confusing thing though is that this ship was declared lost at sea in a storm nearly three decades ago, without a single sighting since until today. Also confusing is that a now major tech company that was only a start up then had cargo on that ship and even though it must be hopelessly out dated now they still want. Given how much effort they are putting into claiming it, they must want it real bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T21:31:19-07:00","id":858135,"title":"","content":"30) Something unpleasant has taken over an oceanic oil rig, but has so far flown under the radar; what it is depends on your game, but the distance from shore is a universal concern. The classic player answer - just blow the damn thing up - would cause a massive ecological disaster and attract tons of attention, forcing them to try and find a less overt fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:00:08-07:00","id":858428,"title":"","content":"31) A small derelict freighter is spotted, potentially about to drift into more populated or more heavily trafficked areas, and the PCs are the ones to respond. The ship is entirely deserted, and all its unusually many anchors have been deployed, and somehow fixed to the ocean floor. Evidence suggests the crew departed swiftly, and the ship has continued to drift randomly since then. Any evidence of foul play is circumstantial, and largely eroded by time and the elements.<br /> <br /> Big Questions: What happened to the crew, how is the ship anchored in place and who did it, considering it's only just been sighted despite apparently having been abandoned for months?<br /> <br /> Bigger Questions: Why are there several pickled body parts in jars and a garbled autopsy snippet of what appear to be a degraded, rotten body full of brine and <i>goddamn sea snakes</i> in the infirmary??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:23:41-07:00","id":858481,"title":"","content":"32) Cannibal rat ghost ship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/web/apparently-this-matters-lyubov-orlova-ghost-ship/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.cnn.com/api/v1/images/stellar/prod/140124131442-sot-atw-ghost-ship-full-o-rats-tompkins-00003522.jpg?q=x_0,y_0,h_720,w_1280,c_fill/w_800\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/web/apparently-this-matters-lyubov-orlova-ghost-ship/\" target=\"_blank\"> Apparently This Matters: A ghost ship with cannibal rats | CNN Business </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/web/apparently-this-matters-lyubov-orlova-ghost-ship/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/web/apparently-this-matters-lyubov-orlova-ghost-ship/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> CNN humor columnist Jarrett Bellini looks into the rat-infested Lyubov Orlova cruise ship that is lost at sea. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:40:00-07:00","id":858497,"title":"","content":"33) You found one of those old-timey messages in a bottle. Judging from the words and conditions of the paper, it's at least decades old. The contents of the message paint a pretty weird log of a ship captain, but something about some of the offhand references strikes you as really odd. It's only later that you realize the captain was talking about historical events... that turned out differently from the history you are familiar with. Did they simply go crazy?<br /> <br /> +) And it seems that was only the first message. Each tide seems to leave another portion of the log in your care, and together the tale they paint gets weirder and weirder. Its clear now that whatever events happened around the captains time turned out differently, or at least the captain thinks they did.<br /> <br /> ++) And now the message are seeming to <i>follow</i> you. You went to vacation miles away <i>and you still keep coming across the bottles</i>. You even went inland one day and found one in a bucket of water.<br /> <br /> +++) The last one left a map. It points to an island nearby. The only problem is - there <i>is</i> no island there, from your experience or any maps of the area. So why is it you seem to see lights coming from the direction the island is located on the map? And why does it seem like the island is getting <i>closer</i> on the map each day you check?<br /> <br /> 34) You find yourself becalmed in a fog one morning. GPS is going haywire and your can't see the sky, let alone the sun or stars. Then the fog starts to clear... and you see a <i>cave ceiling</i> above you. Then an old sail boat pulls up along side you out of nowhere and someone claiming to be &quot;the&quot; Admiral asks what are you doing on the &quot;Ocean of Fragments&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-03-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:44:54-07:00","id":858537,"title":"","content":"A hook in the theme of this thread may or may not be coming in the Beast Dark Era. I think that's the vaguest way possible to say that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:10:54-07:00","id":858901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/846453-100-scurvy-seafarin-salt-soaked-hooks?p=858481#post858481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">32) Cannibal rat ghost ship.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/web/apparently-this-matters-lyubov-orlova-ghost-ship/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.cnn.com/2014/01/24/tech/...va-ghost-ship/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's gotta be one bigass Beshilu by now. Full of disease, having gnawed the Gauntlet thin as paper...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:12:03-07:00","id":860014,"title":"","content":"35) The rip is hungry. The lifeguards talk about it from time to time. The beach should have honestly been closed down years ago, but some vested interests keep it open. Swimmers caught by the rip disappear out to see in moments. Every now and again the lifeguards save a swimmer in time, but there's video footage of the lifeguards that show that they seem to drag their heels, take too long to prepare, so when they get out they find nothing but calm blue water and a body face down. All the bad press has seen visitors to the beach drop sharply in the last few years, but someone keeps trying to drum up interest, get people out there with competitions or events. Someone is trying to feed the rip.<br /> <br /> 36) Six dead humpback whales washed ashore last night. They all had the same injuries. Their eyes were burned out, tongues severed, and a long cut from head to tail along their belly. Marine biologists are baffled as to what could have inflicted the wounds. A few retired police are telling anyone who will listen that those were the very same injuries left on victims of that serial killer who was around in '72.<br /> <br /> 37) The cruise ship blew into town in a whirlwind of music and high spending tourists. There was apparently a staff shortage on board, and a whole bevvy of of young people were happy to grab a chance at a job for a few months and escape their town's ailing job market. Thing is, it's been weeks now, and no one's heard anything from the ones who left. And if you look real close at pictures of the tourists themselves, it's a bit odd how they all have these flaps of skin barely visible behind their ears. Someone suggested &quot;gills&quot; in the pub the other night, and the whole place went quiet. Sure would have explained the smell.<br /> <br /> 38) It seemed like it happened overnight. All of a sudden every lobster pot was being hauled up filled with these ugly skittering critters. Relics of a lost age, from before the birth of humans or lizards or walking things. They've been lurking in their buckets for the last few days, too weird to consider killing for food. The state's environmental agency's been contacted, but no one's arrived yet. The way the creatures move and act is starting to give people the creeps. They're huddled together, but not for safety. It looks like they're planning something.<br /> <br /> 39) The crew of a tanker have been adrift since the engine died two days ago. The ship's engineers haven't been able to get it started again. They've had intermittent radio contact, enough to let the closest port know where they are, but no one's come out to them yet. That's fine, supplies are plentiful, current is basically nonexistent, and the weather has been mild. There does seem to be an awful lot of kelp building up around the ship though, and it looks like it's rising straight up from the ocean bed. The way it moves at night looks like something large is coming to the surface beneath it.<br /> <br /> 40) The <i>Ranger</i> is a navy vessel about to cross the equator for the first time since taking on some fresh recruits. The shellbacks have been busy getting ready for a big crossing the line ceremony, something <i>Ranger</i>'s crew have always taken very seriously. The polliwogs have mostly been shut out of the preparations, but a few were conscripted to haul some big crates up to the main deck. They caught glimpses of the preparations, and boy, it sure seems like it's going to be one helluva ceremony. There are weird grinning masks made of black wood everywhere, and Neptune's trident is so big and old they could have sworn it was the real thing. Captain seemed pretty excited too when he thanked them, and he must have grabbed some contact lenses 'cos his eyes looked kinda... fishy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:03:21-07:00","id":860738,"title":"","content":"41) A Japanese whaler has been found adrift in the Southern Ocean. It is coated with ice, preserving the bizarre scene on its decks. A massive creature is frozen in its death throes, its body resembling nothing so much as a specimen of <i>Labidiaster Annulatus</i> the size of a school bus. Around the dead starfish are the ship's crew, many of them clearly crushed or strangled by its arms. Even stranger, the ship is quickly identified as a vessel still at port back in Japan. The crew members are in a similar position, many of them with the ship, others are people known to be alive and well who could never have set foot on the ship. To top it off, it appears every piece of electronics on the ship has been set to the year 2018. And as the ice thaws and the great starfish's body is unfurled, the salvage crew notice its wounds are beginning to close.<br /> <br /> 42) The mangrove swamp is changing. As the tide levels rise with each passing year, scientists are finding that the local flora is adapting in unusual ways. The shallow water ecosystem is thriving, with underwater cameras showing a great number of unusual adaptations among the species there. Bulbous growths are common in plants and animals alike, and the delicate limbs of the increasingly mobile mangroves twist together into arches and spires that put more than a few in mind of architecture. It takes a while for a detailed analysis to be performed on these rapid changes, but when the results come back they are startling. It is as if the entire swamp has been altered on a genetic level, and the DNA of the living things there no longer match any earthly creature.<br /> <br /> 43) A street gang in Polynesia, total nobodies on the world stage, have suddenly begun to expand their operations globally. In a matter of weeks they have grown from backstreet thugs to masters of international shipping, and no one is able to explain where the money or influence came from. A criminal empire is coalescing out of nowhere, connecting ports in every country across the Pacific. Drugs, firearms, and illicit goods are pouring through these shipping lanes and law enforcement in every country is powerless to stop it. The best they have been able to do is disrupt a handful of the smaller shipments. A small case of pearls has been found buried within the shipping containers of each of these shipments.<br /> <br /> 44) White worms are showing up along the waterline at the beach. There are thousands of them in the wet sand, just beneath the surface. Besides wriggling between the toes of beachgoers and generally grossing everyone out, they also appear to be having a major impact on the local fish population. Those that eat them, and many local species apparently consider them a delicacy, begin to grow larger and slower, almost corpulent. They in turn are eaten by larger fish, who begin to demonstrate the same behaviour. A few fishermen have caught some massive specimens in the last few days, but after cutting them open have discovered worms living in the fish's tissue. Citizens are being urged not to eat any fish caught in the local area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:10:53-07:00","id":860743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/846453-100-scurvy-seafarin-salt-soaked-hooks?p=860738#post860738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">44) White worms are showing up along the waterline at the beach. There are thousands of them in the wet sand, just beneath the surface. Besides wriggling between the toes of beachgoers and generally grossing everyone out, they also appear to be having a major impact on the local fish population. Those that eat them, and many local species apparently consider them a delicacy, begin to grow larger and slower, almost corpulent. They in turn are eaten by larger fish, who begin to demonstrate the same behaviour. A few fishermen have caught some massive specimens in the last few days, but after cutting them open have discovered worms living in the fish's tissue. Citizens are being urged not to eat any fish caught in the local area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:30:56-07:00","id":860753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/846453-100-scurvy-seafarin-salt-soaked-hooks?p=860743#post860743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think 14, 23, and 42 have all been me working through much the same concept/theme in a few different iterations, but I did like how 44 came out. Always fun to make seafood and the seaside icky. I call it payback for a lifetime of seasickness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:39:53-07:00","id":861500,"title":"","content":"45) The song of Broken Cliff is a muted choir, a gentle susurrus of the wind through its caverns and the waves breaking far below. Campers and tourists often find themselves falling asleep while seated near the cliffs, lulled into somnolence by the sound. They usually dismiss the vivid dreams of drowning that follow when they wake, gasping for air. Those who stay on the cusp of sleep experience a sensation alike to the water closing just over their head, a creeping darkness on the edge of vision as they struggle to stay on the surface of consciousness. Of course, this is all the product of active imaginations and proximity to the oceans. The song is just the wind.<br /> <br /> Just don't sleep too long.<br /> <br /> 46) Michael Koppton found the most beautiful shell in the entire ocean, just walking along the beach. It was a stunning thing, a curling spiral of vibrant colours that shimmered in the light. Then his wife stabbed him to death, and she was caught with only the shell in her permission. Then the shell vanished from the evidence lock-up, and the arresting officers disappeared without a trace. When the shell resurfaces it was lying by the body of a coast guard officer with a broken neck, aboard a patrol boat he had taken out without permission.<br /> <br /> 47) The sand island offshore is only a few years old. A change in local currents built it up in a matter of months. The local bird population has avoided it completely, even though it would make the perfect nesting ground. They won't even fly directly over it. And to be fair, they're not the only ones who get an uneasy feeling from the island. The way the sand moves, forming mounds or subsiding into little pits whenever a back is turned, is disconcerting. The presence of quicksand on the island has been confirmed, and the currents around the island make it dangerous to swimmers. Local officials are advising people stay clear of it, and that all shipping give it a wide berth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:16:54-07:00","id":861598,"title":"","content":"A modern day Flying Dutchman, locals have reported brief sightings of the ship sailing without lights in the dark. Law enforcement believes it to be smugglers but no amount of investigation has succeeded in determining its port of origin or where it makes landfall.<br /> <br /> \u200bA massive, privately owned freighter that travels the world's oceans, only it doesn't carry freight, just its mysterious owner and his ever growing collection of oddities. Items (and rumors say people) go on board but nothing ever comes off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:51:23-07:00","id":861611,"title":"","content":"50) Glowing waves shouldn't be supernatural. Phosphorescent phytoplankton aren't even that uncommon in these waters, although they're usually only seen when the waves break. Tonight though, tonight the entire ocean is alight. From horizon to horizon, as far as can be seen around the ship, the water ripples white and blue beneath the crescent moon. And then the shadow comes, larger than the ship, swallowing the light as it closes in on the helpless vessel.<br /> <br /> 51) You should have cleaned the gash on your arm before this. Reef cuts are always dangerous. But you forgot, and now the wound is definitely infected. You can see little flecks inside it, yellow and white and red, that kind of remind you of the coral you were diving near when the cut happened. When you go near the tap to wash it out, however, the wound starts to hurt. It gets worse the closer you come to fresh water, until the pain is too much and you stumble away. But the sea, well, the closer you come to that the better you feel. One little soak wouldn't hurt, would it?<br /> <br /> 52) You drowned, and then you woke up. Now the sea is with you, the tides coursing through your brain, waves crashing just behind your eyes. It is old, older than any dry thing, the primeval ocean from the depths of time. And it knows things, for it has seen all that there has been and will be here until life on this planet runs out. You're not sure if the things it is showing you will make you a prophet or a harbinger of doom, but the waves cannot be denied and the truth of future tides must be shared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:25:28-07:00","id":861699,"title":"","content":"53) You've heard of St. Elmo's Fire. It's meant to be a kind of pale 'fire' that dances on the masts of ships in storms. It's not meant to burn on the surface of the sea on a calm night. Or underneath it. You saw the first flame three nights ago. Just one, maybe a few hundred yards away. The second night, there were dozens and they were at most a hundred yards away. Yesterday there were too many to count, bobbing on the waves only feet from the hull. As the sun goes down, the flames start to flicker into life. One catches on the aft deck. The wood beneath it takes on a golden metallic sheen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:49:45-07:00","id":863384,"title":"","content":"54) The local government still hasn't worked out where the order to dredge the bay came from. The matter is currently undergoing a quiet investigation, but it didn't stop the crew from working every day. In fact, there were even reports of them working through the night. The company that employed the men is a total unknown, phone calls to the number listed as their head office go on hold to the sound of something like whale song and are never picked up. The men themselves were impossible to interview. They never left the dredge. A few attempts to go out to the vessel have been turned back by a voice on the radio broadcasting a warning, saying that it is too dangerous to approach. This voice refused to be drawn in conversation, it just repeated its message until the investigators turned back.<br /> <br /> And then, one morning, the dredge was gone. It couldn't be found in any port in the area. As far as government records show, the work wasn't even paid for. Perhaps they found what they were looking for?<br /> <br /> 55) The military was conducting a series of exercises in the area. It was when they attempted a simulated beach landing that everything went wrong. A squall came out of nowhere. Live rounds were fired. Several units claimed they were attacked by unknown assailants. Six soldiers died, another fourteen were injured. The incidents were ultimately cataloged as friendly fire, and no one has been back to the beach since. They say if you stand on a boat offshore when the sun is just right, you can see the shapes of soldiers dying on that beach. If you're unlucky, you might even see what killed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T22:30:57-07:00","id":869947,"title":"","content":"56) A thick grey foam washed in with the tide, coating swimmers at the beach with a sticky grey film. Those covered in felt nauseous and fled the beach, lifeguards closed the beach. The next day they were all back at high tide, plunging into the water despite the protests of the lifeguards on duty. And when the foam came back, it looked like the swimmers started <i>drinking</i> it.<br /> <br /> 57) There's been a shipping container on every freighter for the last six months marked with a strange triangular symbol. It gets waved straight through by customs officials and stored in a warehouse at the end of the dock. And there they've been sitting, untouched, ever since. There was a break-in a few weeks back though, and every week since a different petty criminal has shown up floating in the harbour in front of the warehouse. It's happened every Sunday since, like clockwork.<br /> <br /> 58) Has anyone ever been up to the fish farm just round the head? I was passing by the other day and saw a couple of workers knocking off at the end of the day. No one I recognised from town though, which got me thinking. There's only a few hundred of us living in this place. So who is it breeding the fish up there? And does anyone actually know what they're breeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:04:22-07:00","id":1385170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/846453-100-scurvy-seafarin-salt-soaked-hooks?p=857663#post857663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Azahul: Now what if an eye the size of your boat opens on the atoll?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would head back to the boat immediately, practically pissing and crapping myself all the way, assuming that I hadn't already left.<br /> <br /> Ya' know... this could also be used as a place to put Story Hooks for <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/SirenTheDrowning\" target=\"_blank\">Siren:</a> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/nwod-siren-the-surfacing-fan-game-brainstorm.678032/\" target=\"_blank\">The</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\">Drowning</a> (originally called Siren: The Surfacing), <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/LeviathanTheTempest\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan:</a> <a href=\"https://wiki.rpg.net/index.php/LeviathanTempest:Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">The</a> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/leviathan-the-tempest-cooperative-fan-project.372576/\" target=\"_blank\">Tempest</a> and its sequel <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles\">Leviathan: The Cult Chronicles</a> (along with another fan-splat that was inspired by The Little Mermaid that I can't recall the name of), since I'm not really aware of any threads dedicated to such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T20:55:16-07:00","id":1385181,"title":"","content":"59: Someone has stolen vital to the characters' success, and made off to the docks with it, Either charting a ship with the promise of a quick pay day or with their own loyal crew, they're dead-set on one course: Full speed ahead to the Bermuda Triangle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T09:34:33-07:00","id":1400326,"title":"","content":"60: Rumours in the supernatural community are that a male Leviathan of the Behemoth Strain and a girls-only shoal of Sirens have managed to enter some sort of symbiotic relationship via their respective water-based forms. Naturally, you\u2019re kinda skeptical/leery about it. That is, until signs of their handiwork start cropping up in (your/the nearby) seaside village/town/city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T11:47:12-08:00","id":1433636,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the Shanty known as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-KO7cofMJH0\" target=\"_blank\">Wellerman</a><br /> <br /> 61: The story of the Billy of Tea is known far and wide in the verses of the Wellerman shanty. Now, Sirens, Leviathans and other supernaturals with a shore-bound territory have started to report sightings of an ancient, 19th century era ship appearing in distant banks of fog, being pulled along by what can only be described as the most perfect blue whale specimen to ever exist. And painted onto the ship's bow are the, albeit faded, words 'Billy of Tea'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}